From a5de419ee96731a762c41782e01b375d08bd167e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: lb-fes <liubing851@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 9 Sep 2026 10:25:53 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix: light-mode tooltip text invisible, dark-mode hardcoded
 colors, task-list checkbox alignment

- Fix #1: .ty-tooltip bound its background to --side-bar-bg-color, which is
  nearly white in light mode, making the white tooltip text invisible.
  Introduce --ty-tooltip-bg-color (dark gray in light mode, unchanged in dark).
- Variable-ize hardcoded light-mode colors so dark mode renders correctly:
  YAML meta block (--meta-block-bg-color/--meta-block-color) and
  .md-mathjax-midline (--mathjax-midline-bg-color).
- Fix task-list checkbox misalignment: global p { line-height: 2 } stretched
  the line box above the text's visual center; restore line-height 1.6 for
  paragraphs inside .md-task-list-item (matches the built-in GitHub theme).
- Remove dead CodeMirror rules (.cm-s-inner.cm-atom / .cm-comment) that could
  never match.
- Migrate deprecated Sass @import to @use.
- Style housekeeping: tabs to spaces in vsc-scheme.scss, lowercase hex colors,
  .editorconfig end_of_line now matches the repo (lf).
- README: replace machine-specific theme path with a placeholder and document
  theme folder locations for Windows/macOS/Linux.
- Include compiled light-and-dark-lb.css for users who prefer not to run Sass.
